---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/lc/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/lc/Footer.astro';
import Container from '../components/lc/Container.astro';
import Label from '../components/lc/Label.astro';
import { facts, rangeProse } from '../data/facts';

// Every number, title, name and date below comes from src/data/facts.ts.
// Do not retype one here - npm run check:facts will fail the build.
//
// RESOLVED 2026-07-28/29:
// - Education: all four credentials are from Universidad Tecnológica de Panamá
//   (confirmed by Luis). Full record, incl. dates, also lives in experience.astro.
// - AIFE venue was never a conflict: two separate appearances, Bangkok (Nov 2024) and
//   Jakarta (Nov 2025). Both now listed below.
// - Survey stat verified against its source PDF; provenance recorded in facts.ts.
---

<Layout
  title="CV"
  description={`Curriculum vitae for ${facts.person.fullName}, ${facts.current.title}.`}
  brand
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="py-lc-8 print:py-0">
    <Container class="max-w-4xl">
      <div class="mb-lc-5 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-lc-3 print:hidden">
        <Label>Curriculum Vitae</Label>
        <button
          type="button"
          onclick="window.print()"
          class="inline-flex items-center rounded-small border border-tierra px-lc-4 py-lc-2 text-small font-semibold text-tierra transition-colors hover:bg-tierra hover:text-arena focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-tierra"
        >
          Download / Print PDF
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="cv-page rounded-medium border border-tierra/15 bg-blanco px-lc-5 py-lc-7 md:px-lc-8 md:py-lc-8">
      <article class="cv-doc">

        <h1>{facts.person.fullName}</h1>
        <p class="cv-contact">
          {facts.current.title} · {facts.current.school} ({facts.current.campus}) {facts.current.division},
          from {facts.current.startMonth} {facts.current.startYear}<br />
          <a href={`mailto:${facts.person.email}`}>{facts.person.email}</a> ·
          <a href={`https://${facts.person.github}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{facts.person.github}</a> ·
          <a href={`https://www.${facts.person.linkedin}/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{facts.person.linkedin}</a> ·
          <a href={`https://${facts.person.site}`}>{facts.person.site}</a><br />
          {facts.person.nationality} · {facts.person.languages}
        </p>

        <h2>Professional Summary</h2>
        <p>
          I build the systems schools usually buy. Over two years at an IB World School in Chennai I
          designed and shipped custom web applications for curriculum analytics, student health
          check-ins, and automated trip and service-learning placement, while coaching {facts.scale.facultyCoached} faculty
          through AI integration, UDL, and digital pedagogy. More than twenty of my tools were requested
          by colleagues and adopted by name in daily departmental workflows. I pair classroom
          credibility ({facts.vis.title}) with software engineering (Google Apps Script,
          Firebase, React) and a coach's instinct for what faculty will actually adopt. The test I hold
          my work to is simple: does it keep running after I leave the room? At {facts.aisc.schoolShort}, it does.
        </p>

        <h2>Core Skills</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Development:</strong> Google Apps Script web apps and automation · Firebase + React ·
          Google Workspace APIs (Classroom, Sheets, Drive) · PowerSchool / PowerTeacher Pro data
          workflows · Looker Studio dashboards · assignment and capacity-balancing algorithms ·
          Git/GitHub
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Coaching and Professional Learning:</strong> instructional coaching (menu- and
          cycle-based) · whole-staff PD facilitation ({facts.scale.facultyCoached} faculty) · UDL implementation leadership ·
          peer observation models · digital citizenship instruction · co-teaching
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>AI and EdTech:</strong> classroom AI integration (Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini, Flint) ·
          HUMAN Framework co-creator · AI policy and academic integrity frameworks · EdTech
          evaluation, rollout, and subscription management · device deployment PK-12
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Systems and Data:</strong> curriculum mapping and gap analysis · institutional audits
          · process documentation and operations manuals · data governance · vendor portfolio
          management ({facts.misc.vendorSpend} annual spend)
        </p>

        <h2>Experience</h2>

        <p class="cv-entry">
          <strong>{facts.aisc.school} ({facts.aisc.schoolShort}), India</strong><br />
          <span class="cv-role">{facts.aisc.title} · {facts.aisc.secondTitle} · {facts.aisc.startMonth} {facts.aisc.startYear} to {facts.aisc.endMonth} {facts.aisc.endYear}</span><br />
          <span class="cv-note">IB World School, {facts.scale.students} students PK-12, Apple Distinguished School.</span>
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Designed and built the Curriculum Intelligence Dashboard, a web app tracking {facts.curriculum.courses} courses and {facts.curriculum.units} curriculum units across three divisions; deployed to {facts.scale.leaders} school leaders. The underlying curriculum Shared Drive infrastructure was sent by the {facts.people.bevans.title} to {facts.scale.incomingTeachers} incoming teachers as their first onboarding resource.</li>
          <li>Built the Health Office App (Firebase + React) for {facts.scale.students} students: digital check-ins with automated same-day notifications to teachers and secretaries; launched school-wide June 2026.</li>
          <li>Shipped {facts.scale.tools} additional tools by colleague request, each adopted by name: report-comment generators for Science and French, a DT/trip safety consent-tracking system, a gamified EAL progress tracker, an automated placement engine (SEVAI) assigning {facts.sevai.students} students to service activities, and the Discover India engine placing {facts.discoverIndia.students} students across {facts.discoverIndia.trips} trips, delivered with a {facts.discoverIndia.manualPages}-page operations manual.</li>
          <li>Led the migration from Turnitin to Google Originality Reports, saving {facts.misc.turnitinSavings} per year, and set up Google Classrooms for all IB teachers.</li>
          <li>Co-created the HUMAN Framework for ethical AI integration and presented it to {facts.scale.facultyCoached} faculty; ran the "Exploring Tomorrow" AI book club for {facts.scale.bookClubEducators} educators including the Deputy Head and Director.</li>
          <li>Directed the secondary school's year-long UDL implementation: orientation series with an external consultant, a UDL Champions cohort, and monthly cycle meetings.</li>
          <li>Co-led the school's Apple Distinguished School application, from planning through media production and coordination; {facts.aisc.schoolShort} was certified as a {facts.misc.appleYears} Apple Distinguished School.</li>
          <li>Served on hiring panels for MS and HS Principal, Student Support Services Director, and Secondary Learning Coach candidates.</li>
          <li>Co-authored the OTL Strategic Implementation Plan 2025-28; member of the Sustainable Data Systems Council and Innovation in Teaching & Learning Council.</li>
          <li>Spoke at {facts.conferences.aiscTenure} international conferences: Data in Schools Singapore/GESS (Oct 2024) and Kuala Lumpur (Oct 2025), AIFE Bangkok (Nov 2024, co-facilitated a HUMAN Framework session for 10+ international schools) and Jakarta (Nov 2025, co-presented "HUMAN Framework &amp; LEA Tool"), and DEIX Vientiane (Feb 2025).</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="cv-entry">
          <strong>{facts.goa.org}</strong><br />
          <span class="cv-role">{facts.goa.title} · {rangeProse(facts.goa).toLowerCase()}</span>
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Teach fully online, asynchronous-first courses to students across member schools worldwide; competency-based grading with narrative feedback.</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="cv-entry">
          <strong>{facts.vis.org}, Laos</strong><br />
          <span class="cv-role">{facts.vis.title} · {rangeProse(facts.vis)}</span>
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Taught MYP Mathematics at an IB World School; built inquiry-based units aligned to IB criteria.</li>
          <li>Designed and taught a grades 6-12 financial literacy curriculum; served on the DEIJ taskforce; presented at AIELOC Hanoi 2024.</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="cv-entry">
          <strong>{facts.isp.org}</strong><br />
          <span class="cv-role">{rangeProse(facts.isp)}</span>
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>{facts.isp.roleCount} roles across five years: {facts.isp.roleList}.</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="cv-entry">
          <strong>{facts.rabin.org}, {facts.rabin.location}</strong><br />
          <span class="cv-role">{facts.rabin.title} · {rangeProse(facts.rabin)}</span>
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Founded the school's robotics program.</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="cv-note">
          Earlier: co-founded Konekti, a coding and robotics education startup in Panama, where I found my path into teaching.
        </p>

        <h2>Education</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>M.Ed. in Higher Education, teaching emphasis · Universidad Tecnológica de Panamá, 2013-2015</li>
          <li>Postgraduate Specialization in Higher Education · Universidad Tecnológica de Panamá, 2014-2015</li>
          <li>B.S. in Computer Science &amp; Systems Engineering · Universidad Tecnológica de Panamá, 2008-2012</li>
          <li>Diploma in Creative Writing · Universidad Tecnológica de Panamá, 2015</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Recognition</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Formal commendation to school leadership for support of faculty ({facts.people.keogh.name} to Head of School, May 2026): "His support has significantly reduced stress for many of us and has made a complicated process much smoother."</li>
          <li>Described by {facts.aisc.schoolShort}'s Deputy Head to an external AI consultant as "making amazing tools to improve teachers' lives, among his many other activities."</li>
          <li>Colleague survey ({facts.survey.name}): {facts.survey.rating} across {facts.survey.responses} responses, with no rating below 4; {facts.survey.wouldEngageAgain} would engage the service again.</li>
          <li>International speaking: Data in Schools (Singapore, Kuala Lumpur), AIFE (Bangkok, Jakarta), DEIX (Vientiane), AIELOC (Hanoi); the LEA tool was taken up by educators at {facts.misc.leaSchools} schools across {facts.misc.leaCountries}.</li>
        </ul>

      </article>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .cv-doc {
    @apply flex flex-col gap-lc-3 text-small text-tierra;
  }
  .cv-doc h1 {
    @apply font-display text-title text-tierra;
  }
  .cv-doc .cv-contact {
    @apply text-small text-tierra-suave;
  }
  /* Section headings: the small label, as Heading 3 in the brand's Docs template, with a hairline above. */
  .cv-doc h2 {
    @apply mt-lc-6 border-t border-tierra/15 pt-lc-4 font-mono text-label uppercase text-barro;
  }
  .cv-doc .cv-entry {
    @apply mt-lc-3;
  }
  .cv-doc strong {
    @apply font-semibold;
  }
  .cv-doc .cv-role,
  .cv-doc .cv-note {
    @apply text-tierra-suave;
  }
  .cv-doc a {
    @apply underline decoration-barro decoration-2 underline-offset-4 hover:text-barro;
  }
  .cv-doc ul {
    @apply m-0 flex list-none flex-col gap-lc-2 p-0;
  }
  .cv-doc li {
    @apply relative pl-lc-5;
  }
  .cv-doc li::before {
    @apply absolute left-0.5 h-lc-2 w-lc-2 rounded-full bg-barro;
    content: '';
    top: calc(0.75em - 4px);
  }

  @page {
    margin: 18mm 16mm;
  }

  @media print {
    /* Keep the Barro dots: browsers drop background colours in print unless asked. */
    .cv-doc li::before {
      -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
      print-color-adjust: exact;
    }
    :global(header), :global(footer) {
      display: none !important;
    }
    :global(body) {
      background: var(--lc-blanco);
    }
    .cv-page {
      border: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
